<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>SADL IDP · How the numbers did</title>
<style>
{% include "_style.j2" %}
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
th { overflow-wrap: normal; word-break: normal; }
td:first-child, th:first-child { white-space: nowrap; }
.glossary { padding-left: 4px; } .glossary li { margin: 6px 0; }
.scroll table { min-width: 520px; }
.scroll td:first-child, .scroll th:first-child { position: sticky; left: 0; background: var(--card); }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.views > label { margin: 0 6px 8px 0; }
.views > label.wk { padding: 4px 11px; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 500; }
{% for v in (s.views if s else []) %}#view-{{ v.key }}:checked + label { background: var(--accent); color: var(--card); border-color: var(--accent); }
#view-{{ v.key }}:checked ~ #vpanel-{{ v.key }} { display: block; }
{% endfor %}.headline { font-size: 1rem; margin: 4px 0 0; }
.calls li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2em 1fr; gap: 4px; padding: 5px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: .9rem; }
.calls li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
.calls li.hit .mark { color: var(--start); font-weight: 700; } .calls li.miss .mark { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 700; }
.calls li.ref { color: var(--ref); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{%- macro f1(x) -%}{% if x is none %}—{% else %}{{ '%.1f'|format(x) }}{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro pct(x) -%}{% if x is none %}—{% else %}{{ (x * 100)|round|int }}%{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro pm(m, fmt='%.1f') -%}{% if m is not none %} <small>± {{ fmt|format(m) }}</small>{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro runs(b, m, n=none) -%}{% if b is none %}—{% elif m is none %}<small>can't tell from one week ({{ '%.1f'|format(b|abs) }} {{ 'high' if b > 0 else 'low' }})</small>{% elif n is not none and n < 4 %}<small>not enough weeks yet ({{ '%.1f'|format(b|abs) }} {{ 'high' if b > 0 else 'low' }})</small>{% elif b|abs <= m %}can't tell{{ pm(m) }}{% elif b > 0 %}{{ '%.1f'|format(b) }} pts high{{ pm(m) }}{% else %}{{ '%.1f'|format(-b) }} pts low{{ pm(m) }}{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro typical(med) -%}{% if med is not none %}<br><small>typical player {{ '%.1f'|format(med|abs) }} {{ 'above' if med > 0 else 'below' }} his number</small>{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro ranks(k) -%}{% if k is none or k.r is none or k.weeks < 4 %}not enough weeks yet{% else %}{% set r = k.r %}{% if k.margin is not none and r|abs <= k.margin %}can't tell yet{% elif k.margin is not none and r + k.margin < 0 %}backwards{% elif r < 0.1 %}barely{% elif r < 0.3 %}weakly{% elif r < 0.5 %}moderately{% else %}well{% endif %} ({{ '%.2f'|format(r) }}{% if k.margin is not none %} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(k.margin) }}{% endif %}){% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro vs(x) -%}{% if x is none or x.diff is none %}—{% elif x.margin is none %}{{ '%+.2f'|format(x.diff) }} <small>(one week can't tell)</small>{% elif x.weeks < 4 %}{{ '%+.2f'|format(x.diff) }} <small>(not enough weeks yet)</small>{% elif x.diff|abs <= x.margin %}{{ '%+.2f'|format(x.diff) }} <small>± {{ '%.2f'|format(x.margin) }}, can't tell apart</small>{% else %}{{ '%+.2f'|format(x.diff) }} <small>± {{ '%.2f'|format(x.margin) }}, {{ 'ours better' if x.diff < 0 else 'ours worse' }}</small>{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro decisions(t, label) -%}{{ label }} {{ t.hits }} of {{ t.decided }} decision{{ 's' if t.decided != 1 else '' }} paid off{% if t.expected is not none %} (the odds expected {{ '%.1f'|format(t.expected) }}){% endif %}{% if t.net is not none %}, {{ '%+.1f'|format(t.net) }}{% if t.net_margin is not none %} ± {{ '%.1f'|format(t.net_margin) }}{% endif %} pts per decision{% endif %}{% if t.wilson %}; the true hit rate is likely {{ (t.wilson[0] * 100)|round|int }}–{{ (t.wilson[1] * 100)|round|int }}%{% elif t.decided %}; too few to judge yet{% endif %}.{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro sm(d, fmt='%.2f', plus=false) -%}{% if d is none or d.mean is none %}—{% else %}{{ ('%+' ~ fmt[1:] if plus else fmt)|format(d.mean) }}{% if d.margin is not none %} <small>± {{ fmt|format(d.margin) }}</small>{% endif %}{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro verdict(d, better, worse) -%}{% if d is none or d.mean is none or d.margin is none or d.weeks < 4 %}can't tell yet{% elif d.mean - d.margin > 0 %}{{ better }}{% elif d.mean + d.margin < 0 %}{{ worse }}{% else %}can't tell apart yet{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro board(sb) -%}
  {% set a = sb['all'] %}{% set ours = a.rows|selectattr('key', 'equalto', 'form')|first %}{% set t = a.timing %}
  <section aria-labelledby="board-h">
    <h2 id="board-h">Do the picks rank the waiver pool right?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p class="headline">Among the {{ s.depth }} players each position showed you, our number ranked them {{ verdict(ours.vs_sleeper, 'better than Sleeper alone', 'worse than Sleeper alone') }} ({{ sm(ours.vs_sleeper, plus=true) }} in rank correlation, weeks {{ a.weeks|join(', ') }}).
        Our top 3 scored {{ sm(ours.top3, '%.1f', true) }} pts a game above the list's average{% set sl = a.rows|first %}; Sleeper's top 3, {{ sm(sl.top3, '%.1f', true) }}.</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Built up from</th><th class="num">Ranks the list</th><th class="num">vs Sleeper alone</th><th class="num">Top 3 vs list</th><th class="num">Top 5 vs list</th></tr>
        {% for r in a.rows %}
        <tr><td>{% if r.key == 'form' %}<b>{{ r.label }}</b>{% else %}{{ r.label }}{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ sm(r.r) }}</td><td class="num">{% if r.vs_sleeper %}{{ sm(r.vs_sleeper, plus=true) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ sm(r.top3, '%.1f', true) }}</td><td class="num">{{ sm(r.top5, '%.1f', true) }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
      <p class="note">Each row adds one layer to the one above, scored on the same players: the {{ s.depth }} a position showed when you set waivers (weeks 1–4: the rebuilt pages; week 5 had no list saved). "Ranks the list" is the rank correlation between that row's number and the scores, within each week, averaged over the weeks (the three positions count as one week). "Top 3 vs list" is how much that row's top 3 scored above the list's average, counting a player who didn't play as 0, which is what picking him got you. ± is the margin of error (about 95%).</p>
      {% if t.kick_minus_tue.weeks %}<p><b>Tuesday or kickoff?</b> On the {{ t.kick_minus_tue.weeks }} live weeks, Tuesday's top 5 scored {{ sm(t.tue, '%.1f', true) }} above the list's average and the kickoff order's top 5 {{ sm(t.kick, '%.1f', true) }}. {{ t.dnp_top5_tue }} of the {{ t.top5_tue }} Tuesday top-5 players didn't play. Counting only the players who did play, Tuesday's top 5 scored {{ sm(t.tue_played, '%.1f', true) }} and kickoff's {{ sm(t.kick_played, '%.1f', true) }}.</p>{% endif %}
      <details><summary>By position</summary>
        <div class="scroll"><table>
          <tr><th>Pos</th>{% for r in a.rows %}<th class="num">{{ r.label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
          {% for slot in slots %}<tr><td>{{ slot }}</td>{% for r in sb[slot].rows %}<td class="num">{{ sm(r.r) }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}
        </table></div>
        <p class="note">Rank correlation with the scores among the {{ s.depth }} shown, by position. One position over a few weeks is noisy, so read the ± before the number.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro view(v, dbn) -%}
  {% set ss = v.by_slot %}{% set single = v.weeks|length == 1 %}
  {% set live = v.suggestions.live %}{% set reb = v.suggestions.rebuilt %}
  <p class="headline">{% if single %}Week {{ v.weeks[0] }}{% else %}Weeks {{ v.weeks[0] }}–{{ v.weeks[-1] }}{% endif %}:
    {% if live.decided or reb.decided %}suggestions paid off in {% if live.decided %}{{ live.hits }} of {{ live.decided }} live decisions{% endif %}{% if live.decided and reb.decided %} and {% endif %}{% if reb.decided %}{{ reb.hits }} of {{ reb.decided }} on rebuilt weeks{% endif %}{% else %}no suggestions decided{% endif %};
    the number the page showed missed by {{ f1(ss.DL.mae) }} (DL), {{ f1(ss.LB.mae) }} (LB) and {{ f1(ss.DB.mae) }} (DB) points on average.
    {% if v.provisional %}<small>Provisional: stat corrections still possible.</small>{% endif %}
    {% if v.held_back %}<small>Week{{ 's' if v.held_back|length > 1 else '' }} {{ v.held_back|join(', ') }} {{ 'join' if v.held_back|length > 1 else 'joins' }} the season figures once {{ 'their' if v.held_back|length > 1 else 'its' }} stat corrections close; until then {{ 'they are' if v.held_back|length > 1 else 'it is' }} under its own tab.</small>{% endif %}</p>
  {% if v.scoreboard and v.scoreboard['all'].weeks %}{{ board(v.scoreboard) }}{% endif %}
  <section aria-labelledby="close-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="close-h-{{ v.key }}">How close was our number?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>For the {{ s.n_eval }} best-projected players at each position{{ '' if single else ' each week' }} (picked by the plain average of the projection sources, so no number picks its own players), the number the page showed before kickoff missed by
        {{ f1(ss.DL.mae) }} (DL), {{ f1(ss.LB.mae) }} (LB) and {{ f1(ss.DB.mae) }} (DB) points on average.
        {% if not single %}{% set part = s.weekly|selectattr('week', 'in', v.weeks)|selectattr('partial_slots')|map(attribute='week')|list %}{% if part %}Week{{ 's' if part|length > 1 else '' }} {{ part|join(', ') }} {{ 'are' if part|length > 1 else 'is' }} only partly covered (the projections saved before kickoff cover some games only), so {{ 'they are' if part|length > 1 else 'it is' }} left out of these numbers.{% endif %}{% endif %}
        {% set rep = s.weekly|selectattr('week', 'in', v.weeks)|rejectattr('week', 'in', v.live_weeks)|map(attribute='week')|list %}{% if rep %}{{ 'Week' if rep|length == 1 else 'Weeks' }} {{ rep|join(', ') }} {{ 'was' if rep|length == 1 else 'were' }} rebuilt after the fact from saved projections (in full or in part), not shown live.{% if not single and v.live_weeks %} Live weeks only ({{ v.live_weeks|join(', ') }}): {{ f1(ss.DL.live_mae) }} / {{ f1(ss.LB.live_mae) }} / {{ f1(ss.DB.live_mae) }}.{% endif %}{% endif %}
        {% if ss.DL.mae_base %}A simple guess, each player's own average so far, missed by {{ f1(ss.DL.mae_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.LB.mae_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.DB.mae_base) }} on the same players (ours: {{ f1(ss.DL.mae_ours_on_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.LB.mae_ours_on_base) }} / {{ f1(ss.DB.mae_ours_on_base) }}).{% endif %}</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Avg miss (pts)</th><th>Runs high/low</th><th>{{ 'Top-12 hits' if single else 'Ranks players right' }}</th></tr>
        {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}
        <tr><td>{{ slot }}{% if x.partial %} <small>partial</small>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}</td><td>{{ runs(x.bias, x.bias_margin, x.weeks) }}{{ typical(x.median_miss) }}</td><td>{% if single %}{{ top12(x.top12) }}{% if x.top12_random %} <small>(random: {{ f1(x.top12_random[0]) }})</small>{% endif %}{% else %}{{ ranks(x.rank) }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
      {% if single %}<p class="note">Top-12 hits: of our 12 best, how many finished in the actual top 12; "random" is what 12 picked at random from the {{ s.n_eval }} would land on average. How well the order matches is shown over several weeks only.</p>{% else %}<p class="note">"Ranks players right" is the rank correlation between our number and the scores within each week, averaged over the weeks, ± its margin of error (about 95%). "Runs high/low" says "can't tell" when the gap is inside its margin.</p>{% endif %}
      {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}{% set b = x.bias %}{% if b is not none and x.bias_margin is not none and b|abs > x.bias_margin and b|abs >= 1 %}
      <p class="note">{{ slot }} numbers run about {{ '%.1f'|format(b|abs) }} pts {{ 'high' if b > 0 else 'low' }} on average{% set med = x.median_miss %}{% if med is not none and (med|abs < b|abs or (med > 0) != (-b > 0)) %}, but the typical {{ slot }} landed {{ '%.1f'|format(med|abs) }} {{ 'above' if med > 0 else 'below' }} his number: a few big games pull the average{% endif %}. Suggestions only compare {{ slot }}s with other {{ slot }}s, so a shift shared by all of them changes no suggestion; it isn't corrected.</p>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% if dbn and dbn.show %}<p class="note dbnote"><b>DBs:</b> so far this season, among the {{ s.depth }} DBs shown, our order barely matches the order of the scores (r {% if dbn.r is not none %}{{ '%.2f'|format(dbn.r) }}{% if dbn.margin is not none %} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(dbn.margin) }}{% endif %}{% else %}not measured yet{% endif %}; last season's waiver DBs: 0.01). Treat DB tiers as rough. A DB's snap share and form, both in his breakdown on the main page, say more than a point or two of projection.</p>{% endif %}
      <details><summary>Our number against simpler versions of it</summary>
        <p class="note">The same players scored three ways: the number the page showed; the same number before the form term ("before form"); and the plain average of the projection sources (Sleeper and ESPN), which this page used to grade until 2026-11-17. The difference is ours minus the other, week by week, ± its margin of error.</p>
        <div class="scroll"><table>
          <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Ours</th><th class="num">Before form</th><th>Ours − before form</th><th class="num">Plain average</th><th>Ours − plain average</th></tr>
          {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}
          <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.ref.base.mae) }}</td><td>{{ vs(x.ref.base) }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.ref.plain.mae) }}</td><td>{{ vs(x.ref.plain) }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </table></div>
      </details>
      <details><summary>More stats</summary>
        <div class="scroll"><table>
          <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Player-games</th><th class="num">Typical miss (RMSE)</th><th class="num">Below / inside / above the range (aim 20 / 60 / 20)</th><th class="num">Spread check (aim 1.00)</th><th class="num">Top-12 hits (random)</th></tr>
          {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}{% set c = x.coverage %}
          <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ x.n }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.rmse) }}</td><td class="num">{% if c %}{{ pct(c.below) }} / {{ pct(c.inside) }} / {{ pct(c.above) }} <small>({{ c.n }})</small>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{% if c and c.spread is not none %}{{ '%.2f'|format(c.spread) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ top12(x.top12) }}{% if x.top12_random %} <small>({{ f1(x.top12_random[0]) }} ± {{ f1(2 * x.top12_random[1]) }})</small>{% endif %}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </table></div>
        <p class="note">The range is each card's floor to ceiling; it is meant to catch 3 games in 5, with 1 in 5 below and 1 in 5 above. Weeks before the cards had a range (1–4) aren't counted. The spread check compares the misses with the stated spread: 1.00 means the odds are as sure as they should be, above 1 overconfident, below 1 too timid.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% set srcs = v.by_source or {} %}
  {% if srcs|length > 1 %}
  <section aria-labelledby="src-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="src-h-{{ v.key }}">Each source on the same players</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>The players are picked by the plain average of the projections, so no source chooses its own. Each source is scored on the ones it projected; "Covered" is how many of them that was.{% set mid = [] %}{% for w in s.weekly if w.week in v.weeks %}{% for name in w.joined_midweek or [] %}{% set _ = mid.append(s.source_labels.get(name, name) ~ ' in week ' ~ w.week) %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% if mid %} A source first read live partway through a week only covers the games still to come ({{ mid|join(', ') }}); projections for games already played are never kept.{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Source</th><th>Pos</th><th class="num">Avg miss (pts)</th><th>Runs high/low</th><th class="num">Covered</th></tr>
        {% for slot in slots %}
        {% for name, by_slot in srcs.items() %}{% set x = by_slot.get(slot) %}{% if x %}
        <tr><td>{{ s.source_labels.get(name, name) }}</td><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}</td><td>{{ runs(x.bias, x.bias_margin, x.weeks) }}</td>
          <td class="num">{{ pct(x.covered / x.pool) if x.pool else '—' }} <small>({{ x.covered }})</small></td></tr>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <tr><td><b>Our number</b></td><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num"><b>{{ f1(ss[slot].mae) }}</b></td><td>{{ runs(ss[slot].bias, ss[slot].bias_margin, ss[slot].weeks) }}</td><td class="num">100% <small>({{ ss[slot].n }})</small></td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section aria-labelledby="sugg-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="sugg-h-{{ v.key }}">Did the suggestions pay off?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>{% if live.decided %}{{ decisions(live, 'Live:') }}{% elif not reb.decided %}No suggestions were decided {{ 'this week' if single else 'yet' }}.{% endif %}
        {% if reb.decided %}{{ decisions(reb, 'This week was rebuilt after the fact:' if single else 'On the rebuilt weeks:') }}{% endif %}</p>
      <p class="note">A decision is one week, one position and one of your players a suggestion was measured against: several badges over the same player are one choice, so the most likely one stands for it{% if (live.badges.decided + reb.badges.decided) > (live.decided + reb.decided) %} ({{ live.badges.decided + reb.badges.decided }} badges in all, {{ live.badges.hits + reb.badges.hits }} paid off){% endif %}. "Paid off" means the suggested player outscored the one he was compared with; the odds expected the sum of the badges' percentages. Suggestions shown only for reference aren't counted, and a void one (a player who didn't play) isn't either.</p>
      {% if single and v.suggestions.list %}
      <ul class="calls">
        {% for e in v.suggestions.list %}
        <li class="{{ e.outcome or '' }}{% if e.reference %} ref{% endif %}"><span class="mark">{% if e.outcome == 'hit' %}✓{% elif e.outcome == 'miss' %}✗{% else %}·{% endif %}</span>
          <span>{{ e.badge }} <b>{{ e.name }}</b> <small>{{ e.slot }}</small> {{ f1(e.pts) }}{% if e.over_name %} vs {{ e.over_name }} {{ f1(e.over_pts) }}{% endif %}{% if e.p is not none %} <small>({{ [(e.p * 100)|round|int, 99]|min }}% said)</small>{% endif %}{% if e.reference %} <small>for reference</small>{% elif not e.counted %} <small>same decision</small>{% endif %}{% if e.outcome == 'void' %} <small>void</small>{% endif %}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="tiers-h-{{ v.key }}">
    <h2 id="tiers-h-{{ v.key }}">Do the tiers mean anything?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      {% set nums = (v.tiers.DL + v.tiers.LB + v.tiers.DB)|map(attribute='tier')|unique|sort %}
      {% if nums %}
      <p>Average score of the {{ s.depth }} players each position showed when you set waivers (the Tuesday sync; rebuilt weeks: before their first game), by tier and by place in the list, with the number of player-games. Higher tiers should score more.</p>
      <p>{% for slot in slots %}{% set o = v.tier_order[slot] %}{{ slot }}: {% if o.r is none or o.weeks < 2 %}not enough weeks yet{% elif o.margin is not none and o.r - o.margin > 0 %}higher in the list scored more ({{ '%.2f'|format(o.r) }} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(o.margin) }}){% elif o.margin is not none and o.r + o.margin < 0 %}lower in the list scored more ({{ '%.2f'|format(o.r) }} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(o.margin) }}){% else %}no clear order yet ({{ '%.2f'|format(o.r) }}{% if o.margin is not none %} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(o.margin) }}{% endif %}){% endif %}{{ '; ' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}</p>
      <p class="note">The ± is the margin of error (about 95%): one game swings a player's score by around 7 points, while the waiver players a position shows are usually projected within 2 to 4 points of each other. Where two tiers' ranges overlap, the games {{ 'this week' if single else 'so far' }} can't tell them apart, even if the tiers are right. The order line is the rank correlation between place in the list and score, week by week.</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Tier</th>{% for slot in slots %}<th class="num">{{ slot }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {% for n in nums %}
        <tr><td>Tier {{ n }}</td>{% for slot in slots %}{% set t = v.tiers[slot]|selectattr('tier', 'equalto', n)|first %}<td class="num">{% if t %}{{ f1(t.avg) }}{% if t.margin is not none %} <small>±{{ f1(t.margin) }}</small>{% endif %} <small>({{ t.n }})</small>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {% endfor %}
        {% for b in v.tier_buckets.DL %}{% set i = loop.index0 %}
        <tr><td>Shown {{ b.lo }}–{{ b.hi }}</td>{% for slot in slots %}{% set t = v.tier_buckets[slot][i] %}<td class="num">{% if t.n %}{{ f1(t.avg) }}{% if t.margin is not none %} <small>±{{ f1(t.margin) }}</small>{% endif %} <small>({{ t.n }})</small>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
      {% else %}<p class="note">No tiers were saved from before the waiver run {{ 'this week' if single else 'yet' }}.</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro top12(t) -%}{% if t and t[1] %}{{ t[0] }} of {{ t[1] }}{% else %}—{% endif %}{%- endmacro %}
<header>
  <h1>How the numbers did</h1>
  <p class="meta">{{ league_name }} · {{ s.season }} season · <a href="index.html">← back to this week</a></p>
</header>
<main>
{% if not s %}
  <p class="note">No week has final stats yet.</p>
{% else %}
  {% set ss = s.season_by_slot %}
  {% set dbn = s.db_note %}
  <div class="tabs views">
    {% for v in s.views %}<input type="radio" name="view" id="view-{{ v.key }}"{% if loop.first %} checked{% endif %}><label for="view-{{ v.key }}" class="{{ 'wk' if v.key.startswith('w') else 'main' }}">{{ v.label }}</label>{% endfor %}
    {% for v in s.views %}
    <div class="tabpanel" id="vpanel-{{ v.key }}">{{ view(v, dbn) }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="weeks-h">
    <h2 id="weeks-h">Week by week</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p class="note">Average miss of the number the page showed, in points. "rebuilt" = the week's numbers were rebuilt after the fact (in full or in part); "archive" = projections fetched after the week from the sources' archives; "late" = some captured after kickoff.</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Wk</th>{% for slot in slots %}<th class="num">{{ slot }}</th>{% endfor %}<th></th></tr>
        {% for w in s.weekly %}
        <tr><td>{{ w.week }}</td>{% for slot in slots %}{% set x = w.by_slot[slot] %}<td class="num">{{ f1(x.mae) }}{% if x.partial %} <small>partial ({{ x.n }})</small>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
          <td><small>{% if w.provisional %}provisional {% endif %}{% if w.replayed or w.rebuilt %}rebuilt {% endif %}{% if w.backfill %}archive{% endif %}{% if w.late %} · late{% endif %}</small></td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="odds-h">
    <h2 id="odds-h">Are the START/UPGRADE odds honest?</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>For every pair of pool players at a position, we checked how often the one we favoured actually scored more.
        Odds score (a coin flip is 0.250; lower is better): {% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}{{ slot }} {% if x.brier is none %}—{% else %}{{ '%.3f'|format(x.brier) }}{% if x.brier_margin is not none %} <small>± {{ '%.3f'|format(x.brier_margin) }}</small>{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
        {% set o = namespace(better=[], even=[], worse=[]) %}{% for slot in slots %}{% set x = ss[slot] %}{% set b = x.brier %}{% if b is not none %}{% set m = x.brier_margin if x.brier_margin is not none and x.weeks >= 4 else 1 %}{% if 0.25 - b > m %}{% set o.better = o.better + [slot] %}{% elif b - 0.25 > m %}{% set o.worse = o.worse + [slot] %}{% else %}{% set o.even = o.even + [slot] %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        {% if o.better %}Better than a coin flip at {{ o.better|join(', ') }}. {% endif %}{% if o.even %}Can't tell from a coin flip yet at {{ o.even|join(', ') }}. {% endif %}{% if o.worse %}Worse than a coin flip at {{ o.worse|join(', ') }}: the odds there are overconfident. {% endif %}{% if o.even or o.worse %}Treat a 60–75% badge as a slight lean, not a sure thing.{% endif %}
        The ± is week to week: pairs from the same week share that week's surprises, so they count as one week's evidence, not many.</p>
      <details><summary>When we said X%, how often did it happen?</summary>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Pos</th><th class="num">We said</th><th class="num">Happened</th><th class="num">Pairs</th><th class="num">Favoured players</th></tr>
          {% for slot in slots %}{% for c in ss[slot].calibration %}
          <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(c.said) }}</td><td class="num">{% if c.too_few %}<small>too few</small>{% else %}{{ pct(c.happened) }}{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ c.n }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.favourites }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </table>
        <p class="note">"Favoured players" counts the distinct player-weeks the odds favoured: a row resting on fewer than 20 can be one player's one game, so it shows "too few".</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="weights-h">
    <h2 id="weights-h">Who gets how much say</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      {% set hist = s.weights_history or [] %}{% set now = hist[-1] if hist else none %}
      <p>{% if s.sources|length == 1 %}Only {{ s.sources[0].name }} so far: it's 100% of every number.{% else %}Each source's share of a player's number when every source has him{% if now %} this week (week {{ now.week }}){% endif %}: {% if now %}{% for name, sh in now.shares.items() %}{{ name }} {{ pct(sh) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}{% for x in s.sources %}{{ x.name }} {{ pct(x.share) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}. Where a source has nothing for a player, the others' shares grow to fill its place. A ranking becomes points by giving rank N the Nth-best projection among the players it ranks.{% endif %}</p>
      <p>{% if now and now.method == 'accuracy' %}The shares follow each source's measured accuracy on weeks {{ now.from_weeks|join(', ') }}{% if now.alpha_hat is not none %}; the best mix of projections and rankings on those weeks was {{ pct(now.alpha_hat) }} projections (capped at 20–80%){% endif %}. Every estimate is pulled toward the starting shares (projections {{ pct(s.prior_split) }}, sources equal within each group) until it has many weeks behind it, so one odd week moves little.{% else %}{% set has_rank = s.sources|selectattr('kind', 'equalto', 'rank')|list %}These are the starting shares: {% if has_rank %}projections {{ pct(s.prior_split) }}, rankings {{ pct(1 - s.prior_split) }}, sources equal within each group{% else %}sources equal{% endif %}.{% if now and now.reason %} ({{ now.reason|capitalize }}.){% endif %} From 3 scored weeks on, each source's share follows its measured accuracy.{% endif %} A week uses results up to two weeks before it, and its shares are fixed at its first sync, so they never change under a page you've already seen.</p>
      {% set wn = s.weights_now %}{% if wn and wn.alpha_hat is not none %}
      <p>Measured on every settled week so far ({{ wn.weeks|join(', ') }}), the best mix was {{ pct(wn.alpha_hat) }} projections{% if wn.alpha_margin is not none %} ± {{ (wn.alpha_margin * 100)|round|int }} points{% endif %}{% if wn.alpha_margin is not none and (wn.alpha_hat - wn.prior_split)|abs <= wn.alpha_margin %}: the projection : ranking split isn't distinguishable from the {{ pct(wn.prior_split) }} starting point{% endif %}.
        {% if wn.sources %}Each source's error against the blend (1.00 = as good as the blend; lower is better): {% for name, x in wn.sources.items() %}{{ name }} {{ '%.2f'|format(x.mean_r) }}{% if x.margin is not none %} <small>± {{ '%.2f'|format(x.margin) }}{% if x.mean_r - x.margin > 1 %}, worse than the blend{% elif x.mean_r + x.margin < 1 %}, better than the blend{% endif %}</small>{% endif %}{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if hist|length > 1 %}
      <details><summary>Shares week by week</summary>
        <div class="scroll"><table>
          {% set names = hist|map(attribute='shares')|map('list')|sum(start=[])|unique|list %}
          <tr><th>Wk</th>{% for n in names %}<th class="num">{{ n }}</th>{% endfor %}<th>Set by</th></tr>
          {% for h in hist %}
          <tr><td>{{ h.week }}</td>{% for n in names %}<td class="num">{% if n in h.shares %}{{ pct(h.shares[n]) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}<td><small>{% if h.method == 'accuracy' %}accuracy (weeks {{ h.from_weeks|join(', ') }}){% else %}starting shares{% endif %}</small></td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </table></div>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% set dst = s.dst_backtest %}
  {% if dst and dst.positions %}
  <section aria-labelledby="dst-h">
    <h2 id="dst-h">Your team-defense idea: tested, not used</h2>
    <div class="slot">
      <p>{% if dst.passes %}At least one signal passed on last season; see the table. It isn't used until it also helps this season.{% else %}Neither signal helped on last season ({{ dst.season }}, weeks {{ dst.weeks[0] }}–{{ dst.weeks[-1] }}), so neither is used.{% endif %}
        For each position's 60 best-projected players every week, we checked whether a player beat his projection more often when his defense was ranked better by FantasyPros, or when Vegas expected the other team to score less.</p>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <tr><th>Pos</th><th>Team D/ST rank</th><th>Opponent's expected points</th><th class="num">Avg miss without → with</th></tr>
        {% for slot in slots %}{% set p = dst.positions.get(slot) %}{% if p %}
        <tr><td>{{ slot }}</td>
          {% for key in ('rank', 'opp_implied') %}{% set x = p.signals[key] %}<td>{{ '%+.2f'|format(x.per_unit) }} per {{ 'place' if key == 'rank' else 'point' }} <small>({{ 'clear' if x.t|abs >= 2 else 'within noise' }}{% if not x.halves_agree %}; flips between halves{% endif %})</small></td>{% endfor %}
          <td class="num">{{ '%.2f'|format(p.mae.projection) }} → {{ '%.2f'|format(p.mae['with signals']) }}</td></tr>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </table></div>
      <p class="note">Points per place of rank (a positive number means a worse-ranked defense's players beat their projection more) and per point of the opponent's expected score. "Within noise" means less than two standard errors from zero. "Avg miss" is on weeks the fit didn't see. It's re-checked with this season's games at weeks 9 and 13.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <details class="slot"><summary><b>What these mean</b></summary>
    <ul class="glossary">
      <li><b>Avg miss</b>: the average gap between our number and what the player scored. Lower is better.</li>
      <li><b>Simple guess</b>: the player's own average so far this season (players with 2+ games). If we don't beat it, the projections add nothing.</li>
      <li><b>Runs high/low</b>: whether our numbers are too high or too low on average.</li>
      <li><b>Our number</b>: the μ the page showed at a player's last sync before his game (the frozen record), the number every suggestion and tier used.</li>
      <li><b>Ranks players right</b>: how well the order of our numbers matches the order of the scores within a week (0 = no better than random, 1 = perfect), averaged over the weeks, ± its margin of error. Shown from 4 weeks on.</li>
      <li><b>Below / inside / above the range</b>: how often the score landed below the card's floor, between floor and ceiling, or above the ceiling. About 20 / 60 / 20 means the ranges are honest. IDP scores have long tails, so the old "68% within one swing" target doesn't apply.</li>
      <li><b>Spread check</b>: the typical miss divided by the stated spread. 1.00 means the odds are as sure as they should be.</li>
      <li><b>Decision</b>: one week, one position and one of your players that suggestions were measured against. Several badges over the same player count once.</li>
      <li><b>± (margin of error)</b>: about a 95% range, from how much the number moves week to week. "Can't tell" means the difference is inside it.</li>
      <li><b>Typical miss (RMSE)</b>: like the average miss, but big misses count extra.</li>
      <li><b>Top-12 hits</b>: of our 12 best-projected, how many finished in the actual top 12 at the position (ties at 12th count). "Random" is what 12 picked at random from the 50 would land: about 12 × (how many of the actual top 12 were among the 50) ÷ 50.</li>
      <li><b>Odds score</b> (Brier): how good our win probabilities are. A coin flip scores 0.250; lower is better.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>
{% endif %}
</main>
<footer><p>Computed from the weeks saved in the repo; nothing here changes the numbers on the main page yet. Weeks marked "archive" use projections fetched after the fact from each source's archive.</p></footer>
<script>
(function () {
  var el = location.hash && document.getElementById("view-" + location.hash.slice(1));
  if (el) el.checked = true;
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
